{
  "title": "74: al-Muddassir المدثر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُۙ‏(1)\nYAA-AYYOHAL AL-MUDDASSERU.\nO thou wrapped up (in the mantle)! \nقُمْ فَاَنْذِرْۙ‏(2)\nQUM FAANZER.\nArise and deliver thy warning! \nوَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْۙ‏(3)\nWA RABBAKA FAKABBER.\nAnd thy Lord do thou magnify! \nوَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْۙ‏(4)\nWASEEABAKA FATAHHER.\nAnd thy garments keep free from stain! \nوَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْۙ‏(5)\nWAALRRUJZA FAAHJUR.\nAnd all abomination shun! \nوَلَا تَمْنُنْ تَسْتَكْثِرُۙ‏(6)\nWA LAA TAMNUN TASTAKSERU.\nNor expect, in giving, any increase (for thyself)! \nوَ لِرَبِّكَ فَاصْبِرْؕ‏(7)\nWA LE-RABBEKA FAASBER.\nBut, for thy Lord's (Cause), be patient and constant! \nفَاِذَا نُقِرَ فِى النَّاقُوْرِۙ‏(8)\nFA-EZAA NUQERA FIL AN-NAAQOORE.\nFinally, when the Trumpet is sounded, \nفَذٰلِكَ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّوْمٌ عَسِيْرٌۙ‏(9)\nFA-ZAALEKAL YAWMA-EZIN YYAWMUN A’ASEERUN.\nThat will be- that Day - a Day of Distress, \nعَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ غَيْرُ يَسِيْرٍ‏(10)\nA’LAL KAAFEREEN GHAYRO YASEERIN.\nFar from easy for those without Faith. \nذَرْنِىْ وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيْدًا ۙ‏(11)\nZARNEAA WA MAN KHALAQTU WAHEEDAN.\nLeave Me alone, (to deal) with the (creature) whom I created (bare and) alone!- \nوَّجَعَلْتُ لَهٗ مَالًا مَّمْدُوْدًا ۙ‏(12)\nWWAJAA’ALTU LAHU MAALAWN MMAMDOODAN.\nTo whom I granted resources in abundance, \nوَّبَنِيْنَ شُهُوْدًا ۙ‏(13)\nWWABANEENA SHUHOODAN.\nAnd sons to be by his side!- \nوَّمَهَّدتُّ لَهٗ تَمْهِيْدًا ۙ‏(14)\nWWAMAHHADTTU LAHU TAMHEEDAN.\nTo whom I made (life) smooth and comfortable! \nثُمَّ يَطْمَعُ اَنْ اَزِيْدَ  ۙ‏(15)\nSUMMA YATMAU’U AN AAZEEDA.\nYet is he greedy-that I should add (yet more);- \nكَلَّا ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ لِاٰيٰتِنَا عَنِيْدًا ؕ‏(16)\nKALLAA INNAHU KAANA LE-AAYAATENAA A’ANEEDAN.\nBy no means! For to Our Signs he has been refractory! \nسَاُرْهِقُهٗ صَعُوْدًا ؕ‏(17)\nSAARHEQUH SAU’OODAN.\nSoon will I visit him with a mount of calamities! \nاِنَّهٗ فَكَّرَ وَقَدَّرَۙ‏(18)\nINNAHU FAKKARA WA QADDARA.\nFor he thought and he plotted;- \nفَقُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَۙ‏(19)\nFA QOTELAL KAYFA QADDARA.\nAnd woe to him! How he plotted!- \nثُمَّ قُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَۙ‏(20)\nSUMMA QOTELAL KAYFA QADDARA.\nYea, Woe to him; How he plotted!- \nثُمَّ نَظَرَۙ‏(21)\nSUMMA NAZARA.\nThen he looked round; \nثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَۙ‏(22)\nSUMMA A’BASA WABASARA.\nThen he frowned and he scowled; \nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَۙ‏(23)\nSUMMA AADBARA WAS TAKBAR.\nThen he turned back and was haughty; \nفَقَالَ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ يُّؤْثَرُۙ‏(24)\nFAQAALA IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM YYUSARU.\nThen said he: “This is nothing but magic, derived from of old; \nاِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا قَوْلُ الْبَشَرِؕ‏(25)\nIN HAAZAA ILLAA QAWLU AL-BASHARE.\n“This is nothing but the word of a mortal!” \nسَاُصْلِيْهِ سَقَرَ‏(26)\nSAASLEEHE SAQARA.\nSoon will I cast him into Hell-Fire! \nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا سَقَرُؕ‏(27)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA SAQARU.\nAnd what will explain to thee what Hell-Fire is? \nلَا تُبْقِىْ وَ لَا تَذَرُۚ‏(28)\nLAA TUBQEAA WA LAA TAZARU.\nNaught doth it permit to endure, and naught doth it leave alone!- \nلَوَّاحَةٌ لِّلْبَشَرِۖۚ‏(29)\nLAWAHATUN LLELBASHARE.\nDarkening and changing the colour of man! \nعَلَيْهَا تِسْعَةَ عَشَرَؕ‏(30)\nA’LAYHAA TESA’ATA A’ASHARA.\nOver it are Nineteen. \nوَمَا جَعَلْنَاۤ اَصْحٰبَ النَّارِ اِلَّا مَلٰٓئِكَةً وَّمَا جَعَلْنَا عِدَّتَهُمْ اِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ۙ لِيَسْتَيْقِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَيَزْدَادَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِيْمَانًا وَّلَا يَرْتَابَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ وَلِيَقُوْلَ الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ وَّالْكٰفِرُوْنَ مَاذَاۤ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ بِهٰذَا مَثَلًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُوْدَ رَبِّكَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ وَمَا هِىَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٰى لِلْبَشَرِ‏(31)\nWA MAA JA-A’LNAA MASALAN NAAR ILLAA MALAAA-EKATAN WA MAA JA-A’LNAA E’EDDATAHUM ILLAA FETNATAN LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO LEESTAYQENA LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA WAYAZDAADA LAZEENA AAMANOO EEMAANAW WA LAA YARTAABA LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA WAL MO’MENOONA WALEEQOOLA LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN WWAALKAAFEROONA MAA ARAADA LAAHO BEHAAZAA MASALAA KAZAALEKA YOZILLO LAAHO MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O WA MAA YA’LAMO JUNOODA RABBEKA ILLAA HOWA WA MAA HEYA ILLAA ZEKRAA LIL-BASHARE.\nAnd We have set none but angels as Guardians of the Fire; and We have fixed their number only as a trial for Unbelievers, in order that the People of the Book may arrive at certainty, and the Believers may increase in Faith, and that no doubts may be left for the People of the Book and the Believers, and that those in whose hearts is a disease and the Unbelievers may say, “What symbol doth Allah intend by this?” Thus doth Allah leave to stray whom He pleaseth, and guide whom He pleaseth: and none can know the forces of thy Lord, except He and this is no other than a warning to mankind. \nكَلَّا وَالْقَمَرِۙ‏(32)\nKALLAA WAL QAMARE.\nNay, verily: By the Moon, \nوَالَّيْلِ اِذْ اَدْبَرَۙ‏(33)\nWAL LAYLE IZ AADBARA.\nAnd by the Night as it retreateth, \nوَالصُّبْحِ اِذَاۤ اَسْفَرَۙ‏(34)\nWAS SUBHE EZAA AASFARA.\nAnd by the Dawn as it shineth forth, \nاِنَّهَا لَاِحْدَى الْكُبَرِۙ‏(35)\nINNAHAA LAAHDAA AL-KUBARE.\nThis is but one of the mighty (portents), \nنَذِيْرًا لِّلْبَشَرِۙ‏(36)\nNAZEERAN LLELBASHARE.\nA warning to mankind, \nلِمَنْ شَآءَ مِنْكُمْ اَنْ يَّتَقَدَّمَ اَوْ يَتَاَخَّرَؕ‏(37)\nLEMAN-Y SHAAA-AL MINKUM AN YYATAQADDAMA AW YATAAKKHARA.\nTo any of you that chooses to press forward, or to follow behind;- \nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِيْنَةٌ ۙ‏(38)\nKULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT RAHEENATUN.\nEvery soul will be (held) in pledge for its deeds. \nاِلَّاۤ اَصْحٰبَ الْيَمِيْنِۛ ؕ‏(39)\nILLAA MASALAN YAMEENE.\nExcept the Companions of the Right Hand. \nفِىْ جَنّٰتٍ ۛ يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَۙ‏(40)\nFEE JANNAATIN YATASAAA-ALOON.\n(They will be) in Gardens (of Delight): they will question each other, \nعَنِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(41)\nA’NIL MUJREMEEN.\nAnd (ask) of the Sinners: \nمَا سَلَكَكُمْ فِىْ سَقَرَ‏(42)\nMAA SALAKAKUM FEE SAQARA.\n“What led you into Hell Fire?” \nقَالُوْا لَمْ نَكُ مِنَ الْمُصَلِّيْنَۙ‏(43)\nQAALOO LAM NAKU MENAL AL-MUSALLEENA.\nThey will say: “We were not of those who prayed; \nوَلَمْ نَكُ نُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِيْنَۙ‏(44)\nWA LAM NAKU NUTE’EMU MISKEENA.\n“Nor were we of those who fed the indigent; \nوَكُنَّا نَخُوْضُ مَعَ الْخَآئِضِيْنَۙ‏(45)\nKUNNAA NAKHOOZU LAAHA AL-KHAAEZEENA.\n“But we used to talk vanities with vain talkers; \nوَ كُنَّا نُكَذِّبُ بِيَوْمِ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(46)\nWA KUNNAA NUKAZZEBU BE-YAWMID DEENE.\n“And we used to deny the Day of Judgment, \nحَتّٰٓى اَتٰٮنَا الْيَقِيْنُؕ‏(47)\nHATTAA AATAANAA AL-YAQEENU.\n“Until there came to us (the Hour) that is certain.” \nفَمَا تَنْفَعُهُمْ شَفَاعَةُ الشّٰفِعِيْنَؕ‏(48)\nFAMAA TANFAU’UHUM SHAFAAA’ATU ASH-SHAAFEE’EENA.\nThen will no intercession of (any) intercessors profit them. \nفَمَا لَهُمْ عَنِ التَّذْكِرَةِ مُعْرِضِيْنَۙ‏(49)\nFAMAA LAHUM A’NIL AT-TAZKERATE MOA’REZEEN.\nThen what is the matter with them that they turn away from admonition? \nكَاَنَّهُمْ حُمُرٌ مُّسْتَنْفِرَةٌ ۙ‏(50)\nKA-ANNAHUM HUMURUN MMUSTANFERATUN.\nAs if they were affrighted asses, \nفَرَّتْ مِنْ قَسْوَرَةٍ ؕ‏(51)\nFARRAT MIN QASWARATIN.\nFleeing from a lion! \nبَلْ يُرِيْدُ كُلُّ امْرِىٴٍ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ يُّؤْتٰى صُحُفًا مُّنَشَّرَةً ۙ‏(52)\nBAL YOREEDO KULLO AMREAAIN MINHUM AN YYUTAA SOHOFAM MMUNASSHARATAN.\nForsooth, each one of them wants to be given scrolls (of revelation) spread out! \nكَلَّا ؕ بَلْ لَّا يَخَافُوْنَ الْاٰخِرَةَ ؕ‏(53)\nKALLAA BAL LAA YAKHAAFOONA AAKHERATA.\nBy no means! But they fear not the Hereafter, \nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّهٗ تَذْكِرَةٌ ۚ‏(54)\nKALLAA INNAHU TAZKERAH.\nNay, this surely is an admonition: \nفَمَنْ شَآءَ ذَكَرَهٗ ؕ‏(55)\nFAMAN SHAAA-AL ZAKARAH.\nLet any who will, keep it in remembrance! \nوَمَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ ؕ هُوَ اَهْلُ التَّقْوٰى وَاَهْلُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ‏(56)\nWA MAA YAZKUROONA ILLAA AN YASHAAA-AL LAAHO HOWA AAHLU TAQWAA WAAHLU AL-MAGHFERATE.\nBut none will keep it in remembrance except as Allah wills: He is the Lord of Righteousness, and the Lord of Forgiveness.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Muddassir (The Clothed One)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 56 verses. Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that the person who recites this Surah in his compulsory prayers will attain a rank near the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) in the hereafter and will be protected from any misfortunes in this world.\nIf this Surah is recited daily and then a dua is made after its recitation, then the dua will be answered and the need will be fulfilled. If one makes dua that he wishes to memorize the whole Qur’an then he will not die until he has memorized it."
}
